<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE lm2c-xichang ascent (3DOF sim)</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Long March 2C / unknown payload (Xichang LC-3) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Method: first-principles 3DOF sim (/workspace/trajectory-deck/sim/ascent3dof.py): WGS-84 rotating Earth, J2, US76 drag,
TIMELINE mode: every ignition/cutoff/separation/fairing time is a published hard event; mdot=F_vac/(Isp_vac*g0); thrust SL/vac on ambient pressure.
FITTED (least squares vs published knots): vertical rise 15.00 s, kick 0.928 deg over 10 s, Cd 0.667, payload 322 kg,
gravity turn, then linear-tangent steering tan(theta)=1.1269-0.006990*(t-t_ign stage 1).
Vehicle config: Long March 2C (Ph.3, two-stage) (sim/vehicles/lm2c.json; every number carries a source URL, derivation, or ASSUMPTION).
LM-2C TIMELINE mode: Ph.3 stage data (World Launch Vehicles 2nd ed. 2007) + CALT TYPICAL flight sequence from huijiwiki; all event times hard constraints. Typical sequence, not this flight&#x27;s.
T0 = LL2 NET 2026-11-05T16:00:00Z (window 15:52-16:16Z). Payload and orbit unknown. Event times = CALT typical LM-2C sequence (huijiwiki), not this flight&#x27;s. UNTUNED: no altitude/range knots published.
Target (see launch config): insertion 500 km, apoapsis 500 km, fpa 0, launch azimuth 136.38 deg; payload 322 kg.
Pad: 28.247059N 102.029008E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s (Earth-relative).
T0 used: 2026-11-05T16:00:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.
POST-CUTOFF: after final cutoff T+542.7 s the stage coasts (same WGS-84/J2/US76-drag model) to PAYLOAD DEPLOY T+546 s; rows after cutoff tagged -coast/-burn.
POST-CUTOFF deploy T+546 s (CALT typical LM-2C sequence via huijiwiki: payload separation T+545.7 s (TYPICAL, not flight-specific)): alt 499.97 km, osculating 498.7 x 501.2 km, i 54.173 deg.</description>
